# Never commit original game data or anything extracted from it.
# See CLAUDE.md, "Clean-room boundary". The pre-commit hook enforces this too.

*.win
game.ios
*.unx
*.audiogroup
gml_dump/
oracle/

# Extracted assets
*.png
# ...except the curated sprite set the browser build ships. CLAUDE.md accepts
# bundling sprites (free, non-commercial). 96 sprites / 271 frames / ~1.1 MB,
# only what the fight code references.

# THE PWA ICONS ARE NOT EXTRACTED GAME ART, and the blanket *.png above was
# silently eating them. web/index.html, web/kaizo.html and
# web/manifest.webmanifest all reference icon-180/192/512, so without this
# carve-out the repo ships a manifest pointing at files it does not contain -
# the install icon and the iOS home-screen icon just 404. They survived only
# in thedevice's vendored copy until a vendor mirror with --delete removed
# them from there too.
!web/icon-*.png
!assets/sprites/*.png
# The battle UI draws item and ACT names with a REAL font asset (fnt_mainbig),
# not the digit-only sprite fonts. Same posture as the sprites: extracted from
# the player own copy, free and non-commercial.
!assets/fonts/*.png

# Generated traces — regenerate with tools/run-trace.mjs, never commit
/traces/
*.csv

node_modules/
/build/
/output/

# The stripped served copy, written by `npm run build:web` (tools/build-web.mjs).
# Rebuilt from scratch every run and derived entirely from the source tree, so
# there is nothing here git needs to know about. The SOURCE keeps every comment;
# only this copy has them removed.
/_site/

# macOS
.DS_Store

# AUDIO SHIPS, EVERYWHERE IN THE REPO. Standing project policy
# (2026-08-20): audio is fully permitted in these projects for as long as
# they are not paywalled and are donation-supported only. The old global
# *.wav/*.ogg blocks and their assets/audio carve-outs are gone — they
# were how a new audio directory could get silently starved out of every
# clone, the same failure that once shipped DEVICE_KNIGHT as an empty
# shell. Raw GAME DATA (game.ios, *.audiogroup, dumps) stays ignored
# above — that is a different rule and it does not move.
